Draw-Align-SFT vendors the complete DiffusionOPSD implementation and adapts its full
SD3 training script at draw_align_sft/upstream/trainer.py:
https://github.com/worldbench/DiffusionOPSD
Pinned reference: 9c4c48cdfe5c3fa712d32957345d75fae9295696
Upstream source identifies itself as an external implementation of the paper
"On-Policy Self-Distillation in Diffusion Models", arXiv:2608.24646.
Relevant source: scripts/train_opsd_ri_sd3.py, scripts/train_opsd_zimage.py,
config/opsd_defaults.py. Its Apache License 2.0 is reproduced in LICENSE-DiffusionOPSD.
See UPSTREAM_INTEGRATION.md and upstream_trainer.patch for the integration changes.
The earlier compact mathematical adaptation remains for regression tests;
it is no longer the default OPSD training backend.

draw_align_sft/advanced adapts the same fixed vendor revision's FlowGRPO,
DiffusionNFT and ReFL baselines and its opd/*_open3.py DanceOPD, DiffusionOPD
and FlowOPD objectives to native Qwen-Image-2.1 / SenseNova adapters.
These ports retain Apache-2.0 attribution. Model-specific noise coordinates,
CFG-free execution, teacher validation, data epochs and checkpoint handling
are local adaptations documented in docs/ADVANCED_ALGORITHMS.md.

Qwen-Image-2.1 adapter interfaces and parameterization follow the pinned Diffusers
implementation identified in requirements-qwen-image21.txt and the Qwen checkpoint
configuration. Model weights retain their respective upstream licenses.

SenseNova uses separately supplied model weights, which are not redistributed.
The existing project's differentiable native training adapter is migrated here.
environment/sensenova_u1_validated.tar.gz contains the native source snapshot
used for the recorded validation runs, including its template resource. Its
origin and file hashes are recorded in environment/sensenova_source_manifest.json;
the upstream Apache License 2.0 is in environment/SENSENOVA-LICENSE.txt and the archive.
Reference upstream: https://github.com/OpenSenseNova/SenseNova-U1

draw_align_sft/optimizers.py adapts the Muon Newton-Schulz kernel and update
rules from PyTorch v2.9.0 torch/optim/_muon.py (BSD license), derived from
Keller Jordan's Muon (MIT license). The full notices and source hashes are
in third_party/muon/. An unmodified PyTorch reference file is retained at
tests/fixtures/muon_pytorch_v290.py for offline numerical parity tests.
The local changes add factor-wise LoRA selection, auxiliary AdamW groups,
checkpoint validation, and explicit rejection of unsupported FSDP sharding.

draw_align_sft/rewards/hpsv2.py follows the HPSv2 v2.0 architecture, normalized
image/text score and full-frame light-augmentation preprocessing described in
tgxs002/HPSv2 at revision 866735ecaae999fa714bd9edfa05aa2672669ee3.
Its Apache-2.0 license is reproduced in third_party/hpsv2/LICENSE. The local
preprocessing is differentiable and corrects the max-side224 padding edge case;
scoring uses a frozen FP32 encoder rather than the official CLI's CUDA AMP.
Model resource hashes and the original scoring/transform sources are recorded
by scripts/download_hpsv2_reward.py in models/rewards/hpsv2/provenance.json.
